          "entries": [
            {"id":"ec3376fa-0","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/0","name":"purpose: Color handles allow users to select and adjust c","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Color handles select or adjust a color value along a track or wheel. The outer border is not included in the handle's size.","after":"Color handles allow users to select and adjust colors in a color picker."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-1","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/1","name":"guideline: Transparent colors.\n\nWhen using transparent colo","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Transparent colors.\n\nWhen using transparent colors, the handle displays an opacity checkerboard background to clearly show the level of transparency.","after":"Transparent colors.\n\nWhen using transparent colors, the handle and loupe display an opacity checkerboard background to clearly show the level of transparency."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-2","kind":"document-block","change":"updated","class":"documentation","bump":"patch","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/2","name":"guideline: Color loupe.\n\nThe loupe is a floating element po","fields":[{"path":"content","before":"Keyboard focus.\n\nThe keyboard focus state enlarges the handle to become twice as large.","after":"Color loupe.\n\nThe loupe is a floating element positioned above the handle. It provides a preview that reflects the color currently sampled by its parent color component and disappears when the interaction ends."}]},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-3","kind":"document-block","change":"added","class":"documentation","bump":"minor","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/3","name":"guideline: Keyboard focus.\n\nThe keyboard focus state enlarg","fields":[],"after":{"type":"guideline","content":"Keyboard focus.\n\nThe keyboard focus state enlarges the handle to become twice as large. The loupe is a visual-only element and should not receive focus since it does not provide interactive functionality."}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-4","kind":"document-block","change":"added","class":"documentation","bump":"minor","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/4","name":"guideline: Display combined values.\n\nColor selection usuall","fields":[],"after":{"type":"guideline","content":"Display combined values.\n\nColor selection usually happens using a variety of input methods (color area, color slider, color wheel). The color loupe should display the final output color: the combined values from multiple color inputs. The number of input methods is determined by the color space (or \"mode\"), for example: 2 controls: HSL using color wheel (hue) and color area (saturation and lightness) 3 controls: RGB using unique color sliders for Red, Green, and Blue 4 controls: RGBa using unique color sliders for Red, Green, Blue, and Alpha"}},
            {"id":"ec3376fa-5","kind":"document-block","change":"added","class":"documentation","bump":"minor","indirect":false,"contexts":[],"record":"color-handle/documentBlocks/5","name":"guideline: Color loupe on down/touch state.\n\nThe color loup","fields":[],"after":{"type":"guideline","content":"Color loupe on down/touch state.\n\nThe color loupe component can be used above the handle to show the selected color that would otherwise be covered by a cursor, stylus, or finger on the down/touch state. This can be customized to appear only on finger-input, or always appear regardless of input type."}}
